+We are now starting Phase 3: Baseline Visual Retrieval for the Visual Heritage Recognition and Grounded Cultural Discovery Platform.
+
+First inspect the existing repository and read:
+- README.md
+- docs/architecture.md
+- docs/project-requirements.md
+- docs/dataset-specification.md
+- docs/evaluation-plan.md
+
+Do not rewrite or remove the existing foundation.
+
+Goal:
+Implement a small, reproducible BASELINE retrieval pipeline that can later be compared against a deep visual embedding approach.
+
+Requirements:
+1. Keep the baseline modular and isolated from future deep-learning code.
+2. Use a simple, explainable image similarity approach suitable as a baseline, such as color/visual feature extraction plus similarity comparison.
+3. Do NOT download external datasets.
+4. Do NOT invent heritage images, metadata, evaluation results, or accuracy numbers.
+5. Use only local example/test images if needed.
+6. Create clear interfaces so the baseline can later be replaced by CLIP/SigLIP or another embedding model.
+7. Add a script that:
+   - accepts a query image,
+   - compares it against a local image index,
+   - returns ranked candidate matches with similarity scores.
+8. Add unit tests using small generated/synthetic test images if appropriate.
+9. Add documentation explaining:
+   - baseline method,
+   - feature representation,
+   - similarity calculation,
+   - limitations,
+   - how it will be compared with the deep embedding model.
+10. Do not implement confidence/unknown detection yet.
+11. Do not implement RAG yet.
+12. Do not build the frontend yet.
+13. Keep dependencies minimal.
+14. Run the relevant tests before finishing.
+15. Report exactly which files were created/modified and whether tests passed.
+
+Make only Phase 3 changes, then stop.

