# 2026-09-30 20:19:05.542830
+I want you to integrate Google Gemini Vision into my existing Heritage Recognition project.
+
+PROJECT:
+C:\Users\humai\AI
+
+IMPORTANT:
+Inspect the existing project before modifying anything.
+
+CURRENT ARCHITECTURE:
+- Frontend: Next.js
+- Backend: FastAPI
+- Existing local recognition: CLIP + FAISS
+- Existing recognition endpoint: POST /recognize
+- Existing local recognition must remain intact.
+
+GOAL:
+I want OPEN-WORLD GLOBAL HERITAGE/MONUMENT RECOGNITION.
+
+The system must NOT be limited to monuments stored in the current FAISS index.
+
+For example:
+If I upload a Jama Masjid image and Jama Masjid is not present in FAISS, the system must NOT simply return Taj Mahal because Taj Mahal happens to be the nearest indexed vector.
+
+IMPLEMENT THIS ARCHITECTURE:
+
+IMAGE
+  ↓
+LOCAL CLIP + FAISS
+  ↓
+DECIDE WHETHER LOCAL MATCH IS RELIABLE
+  ↓
+IF RELIABLE:
+    return local match
+  ↓
+IF LOW-CONFIDENCE / POSSIBLY UNKNOWN:
+    send the ACTUAL uploaded image to Gemini Vision
+  ↓
+Gemini identifies the monument globally
+  ↓
+return Gemini identification + uncertainty + heritage information
+  ↓
+use reliable sources/evidence where available
+
+GEMINI INTEGRATION:
+
+Use Google's official Python SDK:
+
+google-genai
+
+Install it in the backend environment if it is not already installed.
+
+Use:
+
+from google import genai
+
+Authenticate ONLY through the server-side environment variable:
+
+GEMINI_API_KEY
+
+NEVER:
+- expose the API key to the frontend
+- use NEXT_PUBLIC_GEMINI_API_KEY
+- hardcode the key
+- print the key in logs
+- ask me to paste the key into source code
+
+I will configure GEMINI_API_KEY myself.
+
+MODEL:
+Use a currently supported Gemini multimodal model.
+
+Do NOT blindly assume a model is available.
+
+Inspect the available models for the configured API key if necessary.
+
+Prefer a current stable multimodal Gemini model supported by the API.
+
+IMAGE INPUT:
+Gemini must receive the ACTUAL uploaded image.
+
+Do NOT send only:
+"Taj Mahal"
+
+Instead send the image bytes/base64/file to Gemini with a structured identification prompt.
+
+Gemini should return structured information:
+
+{
+  "identified": true/false,
+  "monument_name": "...",
+  "city": "...",
+  "region": "...",
+  "country": "...",
+  "confidence": 0.0-1.0,
+  "historical_period": "...",
+  "architectural_style": "...",
+  "historical_overview": "...",
+  "architectural_significance": "...",
+  "preservation_information": "...",
+  "visual_clues": ["..."],
+  "alternative_candidates": ["..."],
+  "uncertainty_reason": "..."
+}
+
+Do not allow Gemini to invent an identification when visual evidence is insufficient.
+
+If it cannot reliably identify the monument:
+
+identified = false
+
+and return a clear uncertainty state instead of hallucinating a monument.
+
+OPEN-WORLD DECISION:
+
+Inspect the current CLIP/FAISS confidence implementation.
+
+Do not hard-code Jama Masjid or Taj Mahal.
+
+The existing FAISS result must NOT automatically be treated as correct merely because it has a similarity score above the current threshold.
+
+Design the smallest safe mechanism to detect possible out-of-index cases.
+
+For example, consider:
+- similarity score
+- margin between top candidates
+- whether multiple indexed images agree on the same monument
+- whether the candidate set appears unreliable
+
+Do\

